G4606.def:
Σιδώνιος, -α, -ον
(Σιδών), 
of Sidon, Sidonian; 
__(a) the region: sc. χώρα, Luc 4:26; 
__(b) the people: Actes 12:20.†

G4616.def:
σινδών, -όνος, ἡ 
[in LXX: Juges 14:12-13 A, Proverbes 31:24 (סָדִין), 1Ma.10:64 A * ;] 
fine linen cloth; 
__(a) as used for swathing dead bodies (cf. Hdt., ii, 86): Matthieu 27:59, Marc 15:46, Luc 23:53; 
__(b) a garment or wrap of this material (cf. ICC, Jg, l.with): Marc 14:51-52.†

G4622.def:
Σιών 
indecl., 
in NT anarth., but in LXX when used of the city of Jerusalem, ἡ Σ. 
(Heb. צִיּוֹן), 
Zion; 
__1. the mountain: in typical sense, of the Church, Hébreux 12:22; of heaven, Apocalypse 14:1. 
__2. The city, i.e. Jerusalem; in poetical sense; 
__(a) of the inhabitants: θυγάτηρ Σ, Matthieu 21:5, Jean 12:15" (LXX) ; 
__(b) in wider sense, of Israel: Romains 11:26; 
__(with) figuratively: τίθήμι ἐν Σ λίθον, Romains 9:33, 1 Pierre 2:6" (LXX) .†

G4625.def:
σκάνδαλον, -ου, τό
(late form of the rare word σκανδάληθρον, see LS, see word) [in LXX chiefly for מוֹקֵשׁ, מִכְשׁוֹל ;] 
prop., the bait-stick of a trap, a snare, stumbling-block (Lévitique 19:14, Jdth.5:1): figuratively, Romains 9:33, 1 Pierre 2:8 (Ésaïe 8:14; aliter in LXX; στερεὸν σκανδάλου in Aq.). Metaphorical, of that which causes error or sin; 
__(a) of persons: Matthieu 13:41 16:23; Χριστὸς ἐσταυρωμένος, 1 Corinthiens 1:23; 
__(b) of things: Matthieu 18:7, Romains 11:9" (LXX) Romains 14:13, 1 Jean 2:10 Apocalypse 2:14; τὸ σ. τοῦ σταυροῦ, Galates 5:11; pl., Matthieu 18:7, Luc 17:1, Romains 16:17.†
SYN.: πρόσκομμα

G4642.def:
σκληρός, -ά, -όν
(σκέλλω, to dry), [in LXX chiefly for קָשָׁה ;] 
hard to the touch, rough, harsh, (opposite to μαλακός); metaphorically, in various uses; 
__(a) of men, hard, stern, severe: Matthieu 25:24; 
__(b) of things, hard, rough, violent: σκληρόν σοι (ἐστι), Actes 26:14; λόγος, Jean 6:60; ἄνεμος, Jacques 3:4; σκληρὰ λαλεῖν, Ju 15.†
SYN.: αὐστηρός, q.v

G4678.def:
σοφία, -ας, ἡ 
[in LXX chiefly for חׇכְמָה ;] 
skill, intelligence, wisdom, ranging from knowledge of the arts and matters of daily life to mental excellence in its highest and fullest sense; 
__(a) of human wisdom: 1 Corinthiens 2:1 2:4-5, Jacques 3:15, Apocalypse 13:18 17:9; σ. Σολομῶνος, Matthieu 12:42, Luc 11:31; Αἰγυπτίων, Actes 7:22; Ἕλληνες σ. ζητοῦσιν, 1 Corinthiens 1:22; σ. λόγου, 1 Corinthiens 1:17; τ. σοφῶν, 1 Corinthiens 1:19 (LXX); τ. κόσμου, 1 Corinthiens 1:20-21 3:19; ἀνθρωπίνη, 1 Corinthiens 2:13; σαρκική, 2 Corinthiens 1:12; 
of wisdom in spiritual things: Luc 21:15, Actes 6:3, 10 7:10, 1 Corinthiens 2:6, Colossiens 1:28 2:23 3:16 4:5, Jacques 1:5 3:13, 17, 2 Pierre 3:15; λόγος σοφίας, 1 Corinthiens 12:8; πνεῦμα σοφίας, Éphésiens 1:17; σ. καὶ φρόνησις, Éphésiens 1:8; σ. καὶ σύνεσις, Colossiens 1:9; 
__(b) of divine wisdom: of God, Romains 11:33, 1 Corinthiens 1:21 1:24 2:7, Apocalypse 7:12; πολυποίκιλος, Éphésiens 3:10 
of Christ, Matthieu 13:54, Marc 6:2, Luc 2:40, 52, 1 Corinthiens 1:30 Colossiens 2:3, Apocalypse 5:12; 
of wisdom personified, Matthieu 11:19, Luc 7:35 11:49.†
SYN.: σύνεσις, intelligence; φρόνησις, prudence, which with σ. make up (Arist., N. Eth., i, 13) the three intellectual ἀρεταί. σ. is wisdom primary and absolute; in distinction from which φ. is practical, σύνεσις critical, both being applications of σ. in detail (cf. Lft., and ICC on Colossiens 1:9; Lft., Notes, 317 f.; Tr., Syn., § LXXv; Cremer, 870 ff.).

G4690G.def:
σπέρμα, -τος, τό
(σπείρω) [in LXX chiefly for זֶרַע ;] 
seed; 
__(a) of plants: Matthieu 13:24, 27 13:37-38, 2 Corinthiens 9:10; pl., Matthieu 13:32, Marc 4:31, 1 Corinthiens 15:33; metaphorically, of an escaping remnant (שָׂרִיד, Ésaïe 1:9; cf. Wis.14:6; Plat., Tim., 23c; FlJ, Ant., xi, 5, 3), Romains 9:29; 
__(b) of men (as γονή; Lat. semen genitale; so in cl.; cf. in LXX, Lévitique 15:16, al.): Hébreux 11:11; metaphorically, of the divine influence, 1 Jean 3:9; by meton. (as frequently in poets), seed, offspring, posterity: Matthieu 22:24-25, Marc 12:19-22, Luc 1:55 20:28" (LXX) Jean 7:42 8:33, 37 Actes 3:25 7:5-6 13:23, Romains 1:3 4:13, 18 9:7-8 11:1, 2 Corinthiens 11:22, Galates 3:16, 19, 2 Timothée 2:8, Hébreux 2:16 11:18; pl. (FlJ, Ant., viii, 7, 6; Flat., Leg., ix, 853 with; 4Ma.18:1; in Ga, l.with, contrasted with sing., see Lft., in l; Milligan, NTD, 105 f.), Galates 3:16; of spiritual offspring, Romains 4:16, 18 9:8, Galates 3:29, Apocalypse 12:17.†

G4690H.def:
σπέρμα, -τος, τό
(σπείρω) [in LXX chiefly for זֶרַע ;] 
seed; 
__(a) of plants: Matthieu 13:24, 27 13:37-38, 2 Corinthiens 9:10; pl., Matthieu 13:32, Marc 4:31, 1 Corinthiens 15:33; metaphorically, of an escaping remnant (שָׂרִיד, Ésaïe 1:9; cf. Wis.14:6; Plat., Tim., 23c; FlJ, Ant., xi, 5, 3), Romains 9:29; 
__(b) of men (as γονή; Lat. semen genitale; so in cl.; cf. in LXX, Lévitique 15:16, al.): Hébreux 11:11; metaphorically, of the divine influence, 1 Jean 3:9; by meton. (as frequently in poets), seed, offspring, posterity: Matthieu 22:24-25, Marc 12:19-22, Luc 1:55 20:28" (LXX) Jean 7:42 8:33, 37 Actes 3:25 7:5-6 13:23, Romains 1:3 4:13, 18 9:7-8 11:1, 2 Corinthiens 11:22, Galates 3:16, 19, 2 Timothée 2:8, Hébreux 2:16 11:18; pl. (FlJ, Ant., viii, 7, 6; Flat., Leg., ix, 853 with; 4Ma.18:1; in Ga, l.with, contrasted with sing., see Lft., in l; Milligan, NTD, 105 f.), Galates 3:16; of spiritual offspring, Romains 4:16, 18 9:8, Galates 3:29, Apocalypse 12:17.†

G4691.def:
σπερμολόγος, -ον
(σπέρμα, λέγω) 
a seed picker; 
__(a) prop., of birds (Arist., Aristoph, al.); 
__(b) in Attic slang, of an idler who lives on scraps picked up in the agora; hence, as subst., ὁ σ., an idle babbler: Actes 17:18.†

G4692.def:
σπεύδω 
[in LXX chiefly for מָהַר pi., also for בָּהַל pi., hi., etc. ;] 
__1. most frequently intrans., to hasten: with inf. (as frequently in cl.), Actes 20:16; ptcp. with indic., Luc 2:16; with imperat., Luc 19:5-6; σπεῦσον κ. ἔξελθε, Actes 22:18 
__2. Trans., with accusative; 
__(a) to hasten, urge on, accelerate (as Hom., Od., xix, 137; Eur., Med., 152; Sir.33:8 (Sir.36:8): 2 Pierre 3:12, R, mg. (cf. Mayor and ICC, in l, but see infr.); 
__(b) to desire eagerly (find., Pyth., iii, 110; Eur., Suppl., 161; Isa 165): 2Pe, l.with, R, txt. (but see supr.).†
